WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.120
Way to go!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.930
Wow, you rolled a double!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.450
Hardly what you'd expect from a beginner, eh?

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.790
All right...

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.930
Even <i>I</i> should be able to score a strike or two...

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.740
Put some spirit into it!

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.880
Steady...!

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.710
1... 2... 3... 4... 5... 6!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.810
Whaaaat?

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:20.950
Nice gutter!

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.720
Hey, what's my score at now?

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.930
Hmm... in six frames so far, you're up to 19 points.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.480
What about Nanako-san?

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.090
68 points, and she just rolled a double!

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.400
Turkey! What a miracle!

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.680
Yahoo!

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.850
<i>Greetings, my dear brother.</i>

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.530
<i>My true brother...</i>

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:49.470
<i>We're well into summer break now, although the heat has let up a bit, at least for today.</i>

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.100
<i>How have things been going for you?</i>

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.960
<i>Father was talking about you the other day.</i>

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.510
<i>Are you really going to study abroad?</i>

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.190
<i>You'll really be going to Germany?</i>

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.030
<i>To tell you the truth, it came as a bit of a shock to me.</i>

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.920
<i>I've only just learned that I really do have a brother...</i>

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.870
<i>...and now you are about to be going off somewhere far away.</i>

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.350
<i>Certainly, that's a big deal to me, but...</i>

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.890
<i>...there's also...</i>

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.170
<i>...there's also the matter regarding Kaoru-no-Kimi...</i>

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.690
<i>Really, at the moment, that's what is troubling me more than anything else.</i>

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:34.650
<b>38. YES....</b>

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.810
This is Henmi.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.420
Ah! Don't hang up!

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.430
I have something I want to talk to you about.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.550
<i>There's nothing that I want to talk to you about.</i>

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.570
I want you to come meet me. I'm over by the station right now.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.320
I'll be in the coffee shop, so come meet me there.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.660
<i>I can't come. Sorry.</i>

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.680
I'll wait for you, no matter how long it takes.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.090
<i>I'm not going to come.</i>

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.430
I'll be waiting.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.680
Goodbye.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.540
Germany?

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.960
Yeah. I think I'd like to go to Germany someday.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.570
Is that your dream, Takehiko-san?

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:48.590
If I keep at my current studies, then someday, I'll go there.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.830
I think that if I go there, I'll find out whether I'm really cut out for this or not.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.920
Takehiko-san, it sounds like your dream will soon be within reach.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.000
I want to become the real thing. The real-thing...

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.210
...like my father...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.090
There you go, talking about your father again.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.730
That's wonderful.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:15.480
It's great, pursuing your dream so devotedly...

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.290
So what's your dream?

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.700
Hmm... what <i>is</i> it, I wonder...

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.110
Hmm... yeah...

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.590
Well, for the moment anyway, I'm really into basketball...

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.390
Yeah...

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:30.280
But maybe... I think that a person's dream should be something really worthwhile...

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.970
Germany...

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.450
When you go there, maybe I ought to come along, too!

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:44.390
OK!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.540
Let's go ride the carousel again!

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:47.480
OK!

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.190
What's wrong?

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.390
What's wrong, Kaoru?!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.370
She's young...

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.410
Considering how young she is, I must say that this is unusually bad.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.630
It spreads more quickly when they're so young...

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:31.900
How many years?

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.040
How many years does she have?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:36.990
The surgery should be sufficient, at least for the moment.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.540
The real problem is the possibility of metastasis.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.430
Five years. If it hasn't come back within five years, then she should be fine.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.890
If she has five years...

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:51.100
If she has five years, then she has a future before her, at least...

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:52.860
Absolutely.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.990
Kaoru...!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:11.460
I'm sorry...

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.670
I'm sorry, Takehiko-san...

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.150
I...

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:19.500
...I might not be able... to go to Germany...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.510
I'm so sorry!

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.550
Kaoru!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.160
I'm... I'm glad you came.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:45.200
Only because you're that kind of person...

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.810
Two, three days maybe...

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:50.490
You're the sort who might just wait here forever.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.250
It's official. I'm going to Germany.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.350
Come on! Come with me!

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.550
I guess your dream has come true.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.890
Congratulations.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.710
Go, live your dream. Please.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.780
Just forget about me...

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.460
My dream is to go there with you.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.410
Find someone with whom you can share your dream.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.300
That is <i>my</i> dream now.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:17.790
It has to be you.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.690
It has to be you!

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.810
Only you!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.560
Kaoru!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:37.400
Milady...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.620
Please excuse the interruption, milady, but...

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.030
...might you know where Takashi-sama is?

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.370
There is a telephone call for Takashi-sama...

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.920
If he is not in his room, then he is most likely out in the garage.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.600
Ah... yes.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:51.940
Thank you very much.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.950
Ah... it's all right, I'll go myself.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.870
Brother, you have a telephone call.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:08.140
Ah! Shoot...

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.420
I'm right in the middle of something important. I'm sorry, but could you handle it, please?

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.960
Yes, yes...

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:16.810
Are you there? I'm taking the call in his place.

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.890
<i>Ah... er, hello... this is Henmi...</i>

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:23.880
<i>I'm sorry, I guess Takashi isn't there right now...</i>

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.490
No... no, he's here...

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:29.570
He has his hands full at the moment, so I am taking the call in his place.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:31.770
I'm sorry.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:35.650
It wasn't anything important anyway; I'll just call back later.

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:38.060
Ah... er...

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.210
...that time, at Rei's funeral service...

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:43.020
...you helped my brother to calm down.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.170
I wished to thank you for that.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.050
No, it was nothing. Really, I felt pretty helpless myself...

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.380
Is that Henmi?

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.040
Thank you.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.110
Sure...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:00.880
Hey! This is pretty unusual, getting a call from you.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.150
Yeah, right! Ha ha ha...

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:07.220
What? You're drunk, aren't you.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:10.970
<i>What's up?</i>

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.170
<i>Has something happened?</i>

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.180
No, nothing has happened.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.920
Nothing at all...

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.530
Liar.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.820
It's about her, isn't it. It's not working out.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.500
Don't try to hide it from me. I know.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.710
Just keep trying, OK?

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:28.520
Somehow, you'll find a way to get her to come with you to Germany.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:34.400
<i>At any rate, I'm going to head over there now.</i>

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.010
<i>The usual place, right?</i>

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.760
No, it's OK. I'm about to leave anyway.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:40.360
<i>No, wait for me.</i>

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.510
<i>That's why you called me in the first place, right?</i>

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.710
<i>OK?</i>

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:44.990
Sorry about this.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.400
OK. I'll be there in fifteen minutes.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.460
Henmi-san is going to Germany?

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.580
Yes.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:58.510
With Orihara-san?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.450
That, I do not know.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.080
I see.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:08.090
Yes?

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.980
Nanako, do you have a minute?

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:11.790
Sure.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:13.960
Homework?

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.970
If I don't take care of it soon, I won't have time to finish it before the new term starts.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.180
You'll be free tomorrow, though, right?

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:21.390
Yes...?

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.930
Could you deliver this to Takehiko for me?

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.670
These are the documents that Takehiko needs for his foreign study program in Germany.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.880
I'd mail them, but I think he probably wants them as soon as possible.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.590
Did you write those for him, Papa?

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.780
Yes, he asked me if I would.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:39.660
How about it? Whenever you have some free time tomorrow would be fine.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.030
Hey now, it's too late to go tonight.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.460
But he wants them as soon as possible, right?

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.270
I'm heading out!

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.200
Nanako!

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.070
T-take a taxi, at least!

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:56.730
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:03.640
<i>Of course I wanted to get these documents to you - and see that smile of yours again - as soon as possible.</i>

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.880
<i>Also...</i>

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:09.610
<i>...I've been thinking quite a bit about you and Kaoru-no-Kimi.</i>

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.450
<i>How will it all work out when you go to study abroad in Germany?</i>

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.730
<i>I think that I need to ask you about it directly, my brother...</i>

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.390
Hey.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.130
Well, look who we have here.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:32.620
Er... these are from my father...

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.130
He had too much to drink. Pretty unusual for him.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.040
I brought him back here.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.700
First time it's happened, really.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.710
He doesn't normally get like this...

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.820
Sorry about this. Could you help me move him to the bed?

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.090
OK.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:59.850
I'm fine... don't trouble yourselves...

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:04.120
I'm fine... just fine...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:05.870
Henmi!

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.780
Enough, already, I'll go...

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.530
I'll go to Germany alone.

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:14.470
You fool, don't give up so easily!

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.850
<i>My dear brother...!</i>

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.100
Please come with me.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.110
What?

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.190
Please, just come with me!

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.930
What's going on?

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.940
I'm in the middle of practice!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:52.140
Come on!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.820
Hey, wait...!

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.900
It's not like Henmi asked us to do this, OK?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.610
Just don't get the wrong idea about that.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.410
We want you to talk to him.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.750
We want you to spend some more time with him!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.180
We've talked enough already.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:12.310
Consider his feelings some more!

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.060
I have! I <i>have</i> thought about him! That's why...!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:17.900
That's why I did what I did.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.980
I... I don't understand, but...

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.990
...I really don't understand all of this, but...

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.740
...Kaoru-no-Kimi, I know that you need to be with my brother!

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.200
More than anything!

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.130
I'm sorry...!

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:32.980
I'm sorry!

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.720
You... you love him, and yet you...

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:44.070
The more she thinks of him, the more determined she becomes to leave him.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.540
That's just the way she is.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:47.480
That makes no sense!

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.290
That just doesn't make any sense!

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.800
Papa, Mama...

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:05.150
Two people... suppose two people are in love...

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:11.630
...but the woman has a life threatening illness...

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.570
Nanako-san...

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:17.390
The woman believes that she has only five years left to live...

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:24.270
Once she knew that, she broke up with the man...

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:31.490
For the sake of the one she loved... for the sake of his future...

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:36.580
She felt that she couldn't risk ruining that future of his.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.270
She felt that it would be best if they led their own separate lives.

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:45.620
Because she loved him.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:50.040
She felt that she was doing it because she loved him so very much...

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.990
But is that love?

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.460
Is that really love?

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.040
Love...

00:15:56.960 --> 00:16:03.930
Love isn't as simple as that; I don't think that we can really know whether their love is true.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:09.290
You can hope to find some sign, some proof that it's real; but you can never really know whether what you see is love.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:16.240
Then why suffer? Why wait?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.510
He's waited for her for a whole year!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.520
A year he has waited, and he still loves her!

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:24.810
But it still hurts him, he still suffers, and now he may be on the verge of giving up!

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.160
He may end up going to Germany alone!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:27.960
Eh?

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:31.590
This is about Takehiko?

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.370
Er... well...

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.820
I see...

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.680
Papa...

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.370
It's real.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:42.570
What?

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:47.000
If this is Takehiko that we're talking about, that love is most likely genuine.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.930
It's all right, isn't it?

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.800
No matter what may come of it...

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:55.950
...if their love is true, then whatever happens will be for the best.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:56.820
Yes...

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:10.000
It might not be too much longer before you fall in love with a boy yourself, Nanako.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.350
But that will be your love, Nanako.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:19.180
A unique thing, unlike anything that you have known before - a true love of your own.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.500
That wasn't the answer I was looking for...

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:25.810
Well anyway, it's time to shower.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.860
So it was you. I thought so.

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:03.340
You are the one who has been ensuring that the flowers are always fresh.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.590
I'm not the only one.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.800
Misonoo-san, Arikura-san, Mariko-san...

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.220
Two or three girls from Rei's class, too...

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:21.110
They all came to change the flowers, each drawn here for her own reasons...

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:30.170
I came here because I wanted to see you.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:42.690
Is it true that you will not be going to Germany?

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:49.120
Yes.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.120
Why not?

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:01.130
It's a personal matter.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:03.130
I don't see any reason why I should have to tell you.

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:19.110
I have no time left.

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:23.800
Most likely, I would end up being nothing but a burden to him, able to give nothing in return.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:28.020
Five years... no, I think that I have only four years left now...

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.020
You have four years.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.770
You have four years!

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:40.850
Think of Rei - living life to its fullest, right down to the last minute, the last second...!

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:42.990
You still have four years left!

00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.800
I want you to live!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.680
Live it with all your heart!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.090
As Rei did...

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:09.520
You have four years! In those four years, anything is possible!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:19.960
After all, in one summer, in one week... you found the love of a lifetime...

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:26.580
To even think that you would hold yourself back...

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:28.990
That isn't like you at all.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.000
<i>That's not like you, Orihara-kun.</i>

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.950
<i>That's not like you at all.</i>

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.850
Whiskey and water.

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:13.590
Nanako-san here said that she just had to see you.

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:20.730
Oolong tea, please - I'm driving.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:22.140
Coming right up.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.450
I'm begging you! Please don't give up!

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:30.210
Don't go to Germany by yourself...

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.870
Don't do it! You can't! You mustn't!

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.880
Did I ever say that I would?

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:40.880
Last time, when you were drunk, back in you room...

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:44.770
I see. I might have said something like that, I suppose.

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:46.240
Let me borrow this.

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.060
No! You can't have that!

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.610
I want to know!

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:57.630
What were you feeling? What were you thinking?

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:00.640
It's all right. I'm fine.

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:01.650
That's a lie!

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:05.670
Sometimes I get depressed and lose my resolve for a while.

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:07.740
Sometimes I consider just throwing in the towel.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:10.830
But only for a moment. Only for a moment.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:12.660
But...!

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:25.860
Nanako...

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:28.810
Do I really seem like such a pathetic guy as that?

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:36.450
A guy so worthless, he couldn't shoulder her pain, who wouldn't even concern himself with her life?

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:38.190
Is that the kind of big brother I seem to you?

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:41.520
No!

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:42.860
Don't worry.

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:49.490
I have finally come to understand just how painful it can be to love someone...

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:55.530
And I am beginning to realize just how wonderful a thing it can be, as well...

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:15.840
When the final day comes, I'll probably be crying out, I'll be so afraid...

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:23.850
When the time comes, will you hold my hand? Hold me tight...

00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:29.550
I will, if these hands of mine are good enough for you.

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:35.590
Of course... after all... you're all I have...

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:01.910 --> 00:25:05.400
In the next episode...

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:10.420
The time of youth has come to an end for Nanako and her friends.

00:25:10.420 --> 00:25:13.700
Kaoru and Henmi have set off for Germany.

00:25:13.710 --> 00:25:15.710
And now...

00:25:15.720 --> 00:25:18.330
...two years later, as springtime again draws near...

00:25:18.330 --> 00:25:22.280
...Nanako receives a letter from Henmi...

00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:25.230
The final chapter: <i>A Lingering Fragrance</i>

00:25:25.230 --> 00:25:29.920
<i>My dear brother... there is no end to my tears...</i>
